WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.119 --> 00:00:10.320
In 2008, Kosovo became
Europe's newest country.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.110
This small state of 1.8 million people,

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.220
emerged as a result of one of Europe's

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.290
most brutal sectarian conflicts
since the Second World War.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.150
It was a conflict that
pitted an authoritarian

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:26.120
nationalist leader, Slobodan Milosevic.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.780
When bombing stop,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.880
then it will be very easy to
continue political process.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.960
Against Western military power.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.630
We must not allow, ethnic
cleansing or genocide,

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.010
particularly at the edge of Europe.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.650
Today, Kosovo is peaceful but poor.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.900
Kosovo didn't only
transition from war to peace.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.080
It was transition now
from communist country

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.480
to a capitalist one,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.620
from a ravaged countryside
to the one being rebuilt.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.850
Kosovo was part of Serbia from 1912.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:03.180
Then, in 1918, Serbia became part

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.770
of what would become Yugoslavia.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.630
Serbs considered and say that
Kosovo is their Jerusalem.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.550
It was a sort of heart of Serbia.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.383
To this day,

00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:16.590
Kosovo is still divided
along ethnic lines.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.720
Over 90% of its population
are ethnic Albanians,

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.070
who are mostly Muslim.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.350
Serbs, who are Orthodox
Christians, account for about 5%.

00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:33.040
This is the southern city of Pristina,

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.460
capital of Kosovo Province.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.910
Throughout the 1980s,

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.790
Kosovo enjoyed autonomy within Serbia.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.190
But the majority ethnic
Albanian population

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.960
wanted more political freedom.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.220
Kosovo Albanian nationalism was growing.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.780
There were demands that
Kosovo become a republic.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:52.010
Kosovo Serbs began to complain,

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.670
saying that they were threatened.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.550
But there was one man standing in the way

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.210
of Kosovo Albanians, Slobodan Milosevic,

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.300
the leader of the Serbian communist party.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.490
Milosevic wanted to keep
Kosovo as part of Serbia.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.980
He rallied the minority Serb population

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.610
and further divided Kosovo.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.220
Slobodan Milosevic used
the Kosovo Serb issue

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.260
to take power and to play
the nationalist card,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.130
which was to propel him to
full power within Serbia.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:30.760
In 1989, Milosevic became
President of Serbia,

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.880
and within weeks, placed
Kosovo back under the direct

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.640
control of his Serbian government.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.640
Petrit Selimi was growing
up in Kosovo at the time.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.490
He and his family belong to
the ethnic Albanian majority.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.350
When Milosevic came to
power, we lost our status.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.850
Our political rights were lost,

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.050
our economic freedoms were lost,

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.230
and our education rights were lost.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.860
As communism collapsed across Central

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:01.920
and Eastern Europe, Yugoslavia
began to disintegrate.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.130
From 1991, its republics
declared independence.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.480
Wars broke out in Slovenia,
Croatia, and Bosnia,

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:12.820
as ethnic Serbs living
in these new countries,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.380
opposed independence.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.590
Milosevic wanted to carve a
greater Serbia out of the ruins.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.760
So he so he sent his troops

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.710
to support Serbs in these conflicts.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.030
During this turbulent time,

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.890
Kosovo's political leadership
declared independence, too,

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.660
but this was ignored by Serbia

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.130
and the international community.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.800
In the late 1990s, a guerrilla group,

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.750
the Kosovo Liberation Army, or KLA,

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:44.920
began to attack Serbian police units.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:48.040
Its aim was to win
independence through force.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.620
It was mixture of excitement,

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.440
but fear that something
big is about to unfold.

00:03:57.012 --> 00:03:59.930
Milosevic sent more
Serbian security forces

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.160
into Kosovo to defeat the KLA.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.260
The Serbian security forces

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.040
and the Yugoslav army were quite brutal.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.840
I mean, the KLA were quite brutal as well,

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.640
but the overwhelming
preponderance of force, of course,

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.820
was on the side of the
Serbian security forces.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:24.170
On January the 15th, 1999,

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:27.160
Serb forces attacked the village of Racak,

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.310
killing 45 Kosovo Albanian civilians.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.550
Racak massacre was a turning point

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:38.140
because as soon as the massacre
unfolded, people were there,

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:41.930
western journalists, observers,
seeing the dead bodies,

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.780
and calling it what it was,
a crime against humanity.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:46.870
As Serbian forces

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.250
retook territory from the KLA,

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.360
thousands of Kosovo
Albanians fled their homes.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.800
The images shocked the West.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.240
At a peace conference in France,

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:02.330
Western powers gave Serbia
and Kosovo Albanians

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:06.990
an ultimatum, accept a peace
deal or face military action.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.040
We're not interested
in a partial agreement.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.860
We're interested in a
settlement that works.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.210
The Serbs rejected the deal.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.230
We are not talking to Albanians.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.950
We are talking to Americans,

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.750
who would like to take our
territory for themselves

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.080
and for NATO.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.500
And Albanians were just excuse for them.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.890
NATO resolved to punish
Milosevic and his army,

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:33.300
and began air strikes on Serb
military targets in Kosovo

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.100
and throughout Serbia itself.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.280
It is about creating the kind of world

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:43.700
where an innocent people are
not singled out for repression,

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:47.100
for expulsion, for destruction,

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.150
just because of their
religious and ethnic heritage.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.330
During the war, my parents, my brother,

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:59.380
fled the neighborhood, were
kicked out by paramilitaries.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.580
They were hiding in the forest

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.620
I didn't know for several
days, are they alive or not.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.500
After 78 days of bombing

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.840
and hundreds of civilian
deaths, Serbia capitulated.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.470
Milosevic withdrew his forces from Kosovo.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.190
NATO tanks rolled in,

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:17.710
and Petrit was reunited with his family.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.150
As Kosovar Albanians returned,

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:26.400
tens of thousands of ethnic
Serbs fled north to Serbia.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.170
It would be another nine years

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.380
before Kosovo finally
declared independence.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.510
Today Kosovo has a rough
and ready democracy

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:42.150
and a growing economy, but
unemployment is high at 33%.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:48.040
In recent years, clashes
caused by ethnic tension,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.240
have erupted on occasions.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.060
Today most Kosovo Serbs
consider themselves

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:54.400
citizens of Serbia.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.170
They don't recognize the Kosovo state

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:58.140
and they don't feel a part of it.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.370
External pressure could improve

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.500
those strained relations.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.500
Both Kosovo and Serbia

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:08.010
are working to join the European Union.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.520
I don't think either of
us would be able to join

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.630
the European Union family

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.240
until we sort out the
issues with each other.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.360
Dialogue is the only
way we can move forward.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.340
If Kosovo and Serbia are to become

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.870
EU member states, their
governments and peoples

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.510
will have to work together
and bury their bloody past.

